WEBVTT

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.143
Tam'vitte...

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.679
Rel mestal!

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.612
Mestal te'iote senve.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.945
Siote ven'suil.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.783
Bekta!

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.925
Tam'vitte,
me'iote sendaya Voyager.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.536
Federation Starship Voyager,

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.045
if you can hear me,
please respond.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.568
If you can hear me,
please respond.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.768
Voyager, please respond.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.140
Come on, Voyager.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.906
I know you're there.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.304
Hello?

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.874
Voyager?

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.749
Are you receiving
this transmission?

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.879
My designation is Mezoti.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.653
You sound a little young
to be working the com.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.216
I'm eight.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.526
I see. Are there any grownups
I could speak to?

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.567
My species is 689, Norcadian.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.568
What species are you?

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.765
That's a complicated question.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.932
Explain.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.738
I don't know how long
I can keep this channel open.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.802
I need you to patch me through
to Captain Janeway.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.275
I'll try, but my height
may be insufficient.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.629
Hello?

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.031
Voyager?

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:04.000
Mezoti, you are not authorized
to be in here.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.908
Are you going to report me
to the Captain?

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.376
Considering this is

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.905
your first offense,
a warning will suffice.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.414
What were my instructions?

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.423
To wait in the Cargo Bay
until you returned.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.719
Why didn't you comply?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.760
You left the children
unsupervised.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.922
Lieutenant Torres required
my assistance in Engineering.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.929
I was gone for less
than ten minutes.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.933
We told her not to deviate
from your instructions.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.401
She wouldn't listen.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.905
When the Captain asked you

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.406
to take charge
of these children,

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.308
you assured her that
you could maintain order.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.608
Controlling them is
proving more difficult

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.704
than I anticipated.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.749
They're highly unpredictable.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.477
Meditation helps
Vulcan children

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.950
to control their emotions.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.112
You might consider...

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.484
Mezoti!

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.580
I'm trying to talk
to the woman.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.557
What woman?

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:58.256
The one transmitting
from Spatial Grid 2369.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.896
She's made contact
with a small ship,

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.097
approximately
three light-years from here.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.835
Alien vessel, this is
the Starship Voyager.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.137
Respond.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.442
Tuvok? That's you, isn't it?

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.540
This is Lieutenant
Commander Tuvok.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.312
Sounds like
someone got promoted.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.250
I want to hear all about it,
but first

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.913
I need to speak
to Captain Janeway.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:32.190
You're a sight for sore eyes,
Captain.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.630
You, too, Harry.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:41.267
I'm sorry, but do we know you?

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:43.434
I'm Ensign Lyndsay Ballard.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.443
I was a member of your crew.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.947
Of course, I'm not surprised
you don't recognize me.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.449
I don't know who you are,
but I'm not amused.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.111
Ensign Ballard died almost...

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.246
It was on stardate 51563.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.756
I can't blame you
for being skeptical, Captain.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:01.487
But if you'd let me come aboard,
I can explain everything.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.165
We'll beam you to Sick Bay.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.329
I'm sure you'll want me
behind a level-10 force field.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:14.134
No offense.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.231
None taken.

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:17.833
I'm just glad to be home.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.070
Captain?

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.513
What do you think?

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.777
She seems to have
intimate knowledge

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:27.183
of this ship and its crew.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.881
I think we should
find out who she is.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.925
Captain,
I'd like to come with you.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.926
I was very close to Lyndsay

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:37.393
and if somehow it's her...

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.260
I'll know.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.698
Harry and I were on our way
to a Class-M planet

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:48.468
in the Vyntadi expanse,
to recover dilithium ore

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.270
we'd detected
a few days earlier.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.709
When we landed, we
realized it was a trap

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.269
set by a Hirogen hunting party.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:55.905
They'd reconfigured a power cell

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.779
to give off
false dilithium readings.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.545
That's exactly what happened.

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:00.551
Go on.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:04.021
Harry and I headed
back to the shuttle.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:07.890
We were ten feet away, when I
was hit with a neural disrupter.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.461
Harry said
my injury wasn't that bad.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.555
He always was a terrible liar.

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:16.363
I tried to get Lyndsay back
to Voyager, but...

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.870
she was already dead.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.565
We buried her in space.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.801
Go on with your story.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.740
I woke up on a ship,

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:27.006
in a stasis chamber
surrounded by aliens.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.412
They told me they'd used their
technology to reanimate me.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:33.247
I didn't believe them
when they said I'd died,

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:36.288
but they showed me visual scans
of my own corpse

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.915
lying in the torpedo casing
I'd been buried in.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:41.458
The Kobali said
I'd been drifting for weeks.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.620
"Kobali"?

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.857
If you ever met them,
you'd remember.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.422
They look just like this.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.263
After the reanimation process,

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.496
they spent months altering
my DNA.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:53.539
They were constantly
scanning me,

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:54.538
injecting me...

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.575
Just to make you look
like one of them?

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.303
That's how they procreate.

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:00.641
They salvage the dead
of other races.

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.375
I was given a Kobali name
and placed with a family

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:04.814
to help me acclimate.

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.818
You were a prisoner.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:08.319
At first.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:15.892
I wanted to contact you
to tell you I was safe,

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.189
but the Kobali wouldn't let me.

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:21.700
They said you were part
of my kyn'steya...

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.600
my...

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:29.903
my past life, and that I
needed to forget you...

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:31.307
all of you.

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.207
So I spent two years
letting my new family

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:37.806
think I'd accepted them.

00:08:37.884 --> 00:08:40.011
When I finally earned
their trust,

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:44.386
I stole a shuttle
and started looking for Voyager.

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:45.822
That was six months ago.

00:08:45.892 --> 00:08:47.917
They've been chasing me
ever since.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:50.155
In spite of her appearance,

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:53.323
I'm detecting traces
of human DNA.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:56.266
I've compared them
with the genetic samples

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:58.098
from Ensign Ballard's file.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.865
They match.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.706
It's certainly
a convincing story.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.869
But your Starfleet training
is telling you

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:07.707
to consider
all the possibilities.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.078
Maybe I'm some sort
of hybrid clone

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:14.051
or a telepath who accessed
Ensign Ballard's memory somehow.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.248
Believe me, I was suspicious
myself at first,

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.154
but I am Lyndsay Ballard.

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:29.992
Until we find evidence
to the contrary...

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.141
welcome home.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:44.915
Captain, could you
give us a minute?

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:46.951
Doctor.

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:01.528
So it's really you.

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:03.262
In the flesh...

00:10:03.336 --> 00:10:05.327
so to speak.

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:20.714
I've missed you, too.

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:32.329
I know you're all
as eager as I am

00:10:32.398 --> 00:10:34.593
to welcome Ensign Ballard back.

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:36.134
She's a fine officer

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:38.466
who's shown a lot
of courage and determination

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:39.765
over the past few years,

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:41.602
and we're lucky to have
her with us again.

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:44.404
So let's do everything we can
to make her feel at home.

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:45.967
Tom and I have already
taken the liberty

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:48.103
of removing Lyndsay's
personal effects from storage.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.670
And whenever you're ready,

00:10:49.749 --> 00:10:51.740
your old shift is waiting
for you in Engineering.

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:52.943
Thanks, Lieutenant.

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:55.112
Before we get ahead
of ourselves, let's not forget

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:56.814
the Kobali are still out there.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:59.881
It seems they want her back
as much as we want to keep her.

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:01.483
We'll need to take precautions

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.255
in case
they track her to Voyager.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.923
I've run preliminary scans
on the Kobali shuttle.

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:07.828
I believe I can adapt
our systems

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.492
to counter a possible attack.

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:10.592
Very good.

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.264
Well, if there's
no further business...

00:11:17.977 --> 00:11:20.639
Thank you for saying
those nice things about me.

00:11:20.713 --> 00:11:21.941
You seem surprised.

00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:24.516
To be honest, I never
thought you noticed me.

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.483
My mistake.

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.385
So, you still playing
the clarinet?

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:35.120
Actually, I've taken up
the saxophone.

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:36.684
Ambitious.

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:38.559
I bet you're good at it.

00:11:38.631 --> 00:11:41.065
You always were my biggest fan.

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:42.896
Please, no past tense.

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:44.230
Sorry.

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:45.895
This is a little strange for me.

00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:47.199
Really?

00:11:47.273 --> 00:11:50.174
It's been a perfectly
normal day for me.

00:11:51.577 --> 00:11:52.509
Deck 2.

00:11:52.578 --> 00:11:54.409
It just so happens
that hearing you

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.675
play music again
is #26 on my list.

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:58.273
List?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.113
Something I made up
to pass the time

00:12:00.186 --> 00:12:01.118
while I was away.

00:12:01.187 --> 00:12:03.246
I tried to think of
everything I would do

00:12:03.322 --> 00:12:04.687
if I got back to Voyager...

00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:06.918
including some things I
wasn't able to accomplish

00:12:07.026 --> 00:12:08.288
the first time I was here.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.225
Like showing up
for duty shifts on time?

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.662
That's #27.

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:20.128
They're here.

00:12:21.507 --> 00:12:24.499
Ah.

00:12:24.577 --> 00:12:26.477
Why don't you and I
have a cup of tea

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:27.807
while the children play?

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.178
Thank you, but they require
my supervision.

00:12:30.249 --> 00:12:31.876
I like your braid.

00:12:31.951 --> 00:12:34.647
I could show you how to do it.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:35.914
Mezoti.

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:38.252
Something wrong?

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:41.088
I've allotted one hour
for recreational activity.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.685
There's no time
for irrelevant conversation.

00:12:43.763 --> 00:12:45.321
It's not irrelevant.

00:12:45.397 --> 00:12:48.195
Adhering to our schedule
will allow us to use our time

00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:49.598
more efficiently.

00:12:49.668 --> 00:12:51.898
We'll be able
to participate in a wider...

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:54.098
...Wider variety of activities.

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:57.236
Fun will now commence.

00:13:00.479 --> 00:13:01.537
Green.

00:13:01.614 --> 00:13:03.047
Grid 313.

00:13:12.191 --> 00:13:13.783
Counter. Grid 10.

00:13:15.828 --> 00:13:18.092
They're cheating.

00:13:18.164 --> 00:13:19.426
How?

00:13:19.498 --> 00:13:21.125
Azan is using
his neural interface

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.100
to share information.

00:13:23.169 --> 00:13:24.431
Is this true?

00:13:26.539 --> 00:13:29.133
You will exercise
Punishment Protocol 9-Alpha.

00:13:37.183 --> 00:13:39.651
If they cannot participate,
neither will I.

00:13:39.718 --> 00:13:42.278
You are encouraging disorder.

00:13:42.354 --> 00:13:44.288
And you never let us do
what we want.

00:13:46.725 --> 00:13:49.751
You will exercise
Punishment Protocol 9-Alpha.

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:52.127
No... I won't.

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:03.434
There you go.

00:14:03.509 --> 00:14:05.704
I can't believe
you saved all this.

00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:08.645
Tuvok thought I should
recycle everything,

00:14:08.714 --> 00:14:11.706
but I just couldn't
bring myself to do it.

00:14:11.784 --> 00:14:14.878
My skates and I thank you
from the bottom of our hearts.

00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:27.493
Do you know how long
it took me to fold those?

00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:30.091
Same old Harry.

00:14:30.169 --> 00:14:32.933
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:36.132
You're still sort of obsessive.

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:38.369
I'm tidy.

00:14:38.444 --> 00:14:41.709
Is that why you used to request
baryon sweeps of your dorm room?

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:44.510
When you live across the hall
from a slob...

00:14:44.583 --> 00:14:45.777
Hey.

00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:47.944
Show some respect for the dead.

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:53.522
Did I say something wrong?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.789
It's nothing.

00:14:56.862 --> 00:14:59.387
Just because I've been gone
for three years

00:14:59.465 --> 00:15:02.366
doesn't mean I can't
still read you like a book.

00:15:03.435 --> 00:15:06.370
I gave the eulogy
at your funeral.

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:10.166
Oh?

00:15:11.977 --> 00:15:13.706
What'd you say?

00:15:15.447 --> 00:15:16.709
Come on.

00:15:16.782 --> 00:15:19.649
It's everyone's fantasy
to hear their own eulogy.

00:15:19.718 --> 00:15:21.845
Absolutely not.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.990
It's probably for the best.

00:15:29.328 --> 00:15:32.456
You always were
a terrible public speaker.

00:15:34.867 --> 00:15:37.392
Just hope you didn't
stutter too much.

00:15:42.708 --> 00:15:45.176
I told them you had
a favorite saying...

00:15:45.244 --> 00:15:46.609
something you got

00:15:46.679 --> 00:15:49.671
from an old Klingon battle cry.

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:52.080
"Own the Day."

00:15:52.151 --> 00:15:55.382
I said that you
always believed in...

00:15:55.454 --> 00:15:57.217
attacking each day...

00:15:57.289 --> 00:15:59.450
possessing it...

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:01.390
and that that was

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:04.054
what made you so much
fun to be around.

00:16:04.129 --> 00:16:07.223
Is that when everybody
burst into tears?

00:16:09.268 --> 00:16:11.202
I said that,
if you'd been there,

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.762
you would have told
them to own that day,

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.365
to attack it, make it their own

00:16:17.443 --> 00:16:19.741
and plan to do
the same thing tomorrow.

00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:25.647
Pretty strong stuff.

00:16:25.718 --> 00:16:27.481
You were a strong person.

00:16:27.553 --> 00:16:29.714
Not always.

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:31.881
These last six months
haven't been easy.

00:16:31.957 --> 00:16:33.925
There were plenty of times
when I could have given up.

00:16:33.993 --> 00:16:35.551
But you didn't.

00:16:35.627 --> 00:16:37.595
You know why?

00:16:39.398 --> 00:16:41.662
You.

00:16:41.734 --> 00:16:43.998
I wanted to see you again.

00:16:47.806 --> 00:16:51.469
Hmm. Guess I won't be
needing this anymore.

00:16:54.146 --> 00:16:55.943
Sick Bay to Ensign Ballard.

00:16:56.048 --> 00:17:01.486
I've finished analyzing
your bio-scans.

00:17:01.553 --> 00:17:03.418
I'm on my way.

00:17:03.489 --> 00:17:04.888
My scans identified

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:07.221
a genetic pathogen
in your bloodstream.

00:17:07.292 --> 00:17:10.557
It appears to have converted
most of your human DNA

00:17:10.629 --> 00:17:12.654
into a Kobali protein structure.

00:17:12.731 --> 00:17:14.323
Is there any way to reverse it?

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:16.368
The biochemical changes
have affected

00:17:16.435 --> 00:17:17.834
every system in your body.

00:17:17.903 --> 00:17:20.872
I'm afraid there isn't
enough of your original DNA left

00:17:20.939 --> 00:17:23.100
to make you human again.

00:17:23.175 --> 00:17:27.771
But I believe I can effect
some cosmetic changes.

00:17:27.846 --> 00:17:29.040
Are you saying

00:17:29.114 --> 00:17:31.139
you could make me
look like me again?

00:17:31.216 --> 00:17:33.047
Yes.

00:17:33.118 --> 00:17:35.712
The alternations would
literally be skin-deep

00:17:35.788 --> 00:17:37.756
and it may take
several treatments,

00:17:37.823 --> 00:17:40.189
but I've devised
an inaprovaline compound

00:17:40.259 --> 00:17:41.783
which should do the trick.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.327
Physiologically,
you'd still be Kobali

00:17:43.395 --> 00:17:44.885
with a multispheric brain,

00:17:44.963 --> 00:17:47.022
a binary cardiovascular
system...

00:17:47.099 --> 00:17:48.430
But I'd look human.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.694
Oh, yes.

00:17:49.768 --> 00:17:52.362
I've lived with this face
for long enough.

00:17:52.438 --> 00:17:53.370
Let's do it.

00:17:53.439 --> 00:17:55.669
Have a seat.

00:17:55.741 --> 00:17:57.902
You may experience
some dizziness.

00:17:57.976 --> 00:17:59.637
I'll hang on to Harry
for support,

00:17:59.711 --> 00:18:01.042
if he doesn't mind.

00:18:01.113 --> 00:18:02.444
That's what I'm here for.

00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:14.491
What?

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.084
Something wrong?

00:18:17.496 --> 00:18:19.657
See for yourself.

00:18:36.949 --> 00:18:38.883
Here we are...

00:18:38.951 --> 00:18:41.749
one Jiballian Berry salad.

00:18:42.955 --> 00:18:45.116
I have been looking
forward to this

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.590
for a very long time.

00:18:47.659 --> 00:18:49.092
It was #6 on her list.

00:18:49.161 --> 00:18:51.288
There isn't much variety
in the Kobali diet.

00:18:51.363 --> 00:18:54.264
We ate the same gray
paste for three years.

00:19:00.005 --> 00:19:02.565
It doesn't taste
the way I remember it.

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:03.835
What's wrong? Too sweet?

00:19:03.909 --> 00:19:07.743
No offense, but it's got
sort of a metallic flavor.

00:19:13.185 --> 00:19:14.777
Seems fine to me.

00:19:16.355 --> 00:19:18.448
I guess my taste buds
are still Kobali.

00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:20.424
Can I get you something else?

00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:21.789
Thanks.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.124
But I need to take care of #16:

00:19:24.196 --> 00:19:25.993
Dazzle Lieutenant Torres.

00:19:33.539 --> 00:19:35.905
One minute early.

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:37.906
There's a first time
for everything.

00:19:38.043 --> 00:19:40.170
An alignment error
has been cropping up

00:19:40.245 --> 00:19:41.610
in the dilithium matrix.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.478
We can't seem to figure
out what's causing it.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:46.711
I-I know that you're
still settling in,

00:19:46.785 --> 00:19:49.151
so I'll give you
a couple of days to...

00:19:49.221 --> 00:19:50.779
It's a vyk'tiote.

00:19:50.856 --> 00:19:52.118
Excuse me?

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:53.852
Oh, a Kobali word to describe

00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:55.689
a certain kind
of wave phenomenon.

00:19:55.761 --> 00:19:57.160
It's hard to translate.

00:19:57.229 --> 00:19:59.163
Try me.

00:19:59.231 --> 00:20:02.632
Literally, it means
"crumpled dance."

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:07.331
All I need to do is vyq'tal
the qen'dioqe matrices,

00:20:07.406 --> 00:20:11.570
stabilize the per'cheya,
tez'tel se nenna...

00:20:11.643 --> 00:20:13.611
Cham'bioque!

00:20:15.414 --> 00:20:16.938
What?

00:20:17.082 --> 00:20:19.778
You were speaking Kobali.

00:20:25.591 --> 00:20:26.956
I didn't realize.

00:20:27.092 --> 00:20:28.354
I'm sorry.

00:20:28.427 --> 00:20:33.524
Well, whatever you did,
the alignment error is gone.

00:20:33.599 --> 00:20:34.964
Nice job.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:36.795
Thanks.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:42.433
I think there might be
a few..."crumpled dances"

00:20:42.507 --> 00:20:44.304
in the warp core, too.

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:46.241
Feel like taking a look?

00:20:52.884 --> 00:20:54.476
Any sign of the Kobali?

00:20:54.553 --> 00:20:55.815
None.

00:20:55.887 --> 00:20:58.321
The latest tactical reports
from Tuvok.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.857
Commander...

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.926
I no longer wish
to serve as guardian

00:21:04.062 --> 00:21:05.495
to the Borg children.

00:21:05.564 --> 00:21:07.498
What's the problem?

00:21:07.566 --> 00:21:09.158
Their behavior is chaotic.

00:21:09.234 --> 00:21:13.261
My attempts to apply discipline
only result in further disorder.

00:21:13.338 --> 00:21:16.432
Well, kids and disorder
usually go hand-in-hand.

00:21:16.508 --> 00:21:18.237
Neelix issued
a similar warning

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:20.301
prior to my taking
this assignment,

00:21:20.379 --> 00:21:22.939
which is why I devised
an activities schedule

00:21:23.048 --> 00:21:24.640
to promote focus and unity.

00:21:24.716 --> 00:21:27.617
0700 hours, the children
emerge from their alcoves.

00:21:27.686 --> 00:21:29.916
Nutrients are ingested
in the Mess Hall

00:21:29.988 --> 00:21:31.956
prior to proceeding
to the Science Lab

00:21:32.024 --> 00:21:33.048
to begin classes.

00:21:33.125 --> 00:21:35.559
At 1300 hours, nutrients
are consumed a second time

00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:37.151
before reporting
to the holodeck,

00:21:37.229 --> 00:21:39.720
where they're studying
comparative alien physiology.

00:21:39.798 --> 00:21:42.460
Doesn't sound like
there's much time for fun.

00:21:42.534 --> 00:21:43.967
On the contrary.

00:21:44.069 --> 00:21:46.435
I've scheduled
recreational activities.

00:21:46.505 --> 00:21:49.065
You can't always
schedule fun, Seven.

00:21:49.141 --> 00:21:51.507
Sometimes it needs
to be spontaneous.

00:21:51.576 --> 00:21:54.409
According to my research,
children require structure.

00:21:54.479 --> 00:21:56.344
I agree,
but not to this extreme.

00:21:56.415 --> 00:21:59.816
You're treating them like
they're still on a Borg cube.

00:21:59.885 --> 00:22:01.910
You're comparing me
to the collective?

00:22:02.054 --> 00:22:04.454
You have all four children
functioning as one.

00:22:04.523 --> 00:22:07.151
They do the same things together
at the same time.

00:22:07.225 --> 00:22:10.251
So that each child has
the same opportunities to learn.

00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:14.661
They're individuals.

00:22:14.733 --> 00:22:16.166
Maybe they're rebelling

00:22:16.234 --> 00:22:18.429
because you don't let them
express themselves.

00:22:18.503 --> 00:22:19.936
Then grant my request.

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:23.168
Choose a more suitable
crew member to instruct them.

00:22:23.241 --> 00:22:24.503
Sorry, Seven.

00:22:24.576 --> 00:22:26.441
Permission denied.

00:22:32.584 --> 00:22:35.553
Well, I see you're finally
going to try my hockey program.

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:37.952
Actually, I'm taking
Lyndsay skating.

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:39.921
Oh. Mm. You two sure
have been spending

00:22:39.991 --> 00:22:41.424
a lot of time together lately.

00:22:41.493 --> 00:22:42.892
Don't start.

00:22:42.961 --> 00:22:44.155
Oh, now, let's see...

00:22:44.229 --> 00:22:45.662
for those of us keeping score,

00:22:45.731 --> 00:22:47.562
Harry Kim has fallen
for a hologram,

00:22:47.632 --> 00:22:50.328
a Borg, the wrong twin

00:22:50.402 --> 00:22:51.596
and now, the dearly departed.

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:53.365
We're friends.

00:22:53.438 --> 00:22:54.928
- Ah.
- Just like before.

00:22:55.006 --> 00:22:58.601
Uh, all right,
maybe there was a time

00:22:58.677 --> 00:23:00.372
when I thought
of pursuing Lyndsay,

00:23:00.445 --> 00:23:01.673
but I closed the door on that

00:23:01.747 --> 00:23:03.374
when we both got assigned
to Voyager.

00:23:03.448 --> 00:23:04.779
Mm. Don't look now,

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:07.045
but that door is creaking open.

00:23:21.733 --> 00:23:23.257
What do you think?

00:23:23.335 --> 00:23:25.895
Uh... you look great.

00:23:25.971 --> 00:23:28.064
Doctor thought I should stick
to my original color,

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:29.402
but this seemed more exciting.

00:23:29.474 --> 00:23:31.237
Hair is one of my specialties,

00:23:31.309 --> 00:23:34.107
despite evidence
to the contrary.

00:23:34.179 --> 00:23:35.407
It's just too bad

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:37.311
that beneath
this beautiful red hair

00:23:37.382 --> 00:23:39.782
still lies the six-lobed
brain of a Kobali.

00:23:39.851 --> 00:23:42.718
Well, are you feeling human
enough for a little skating?

00:23:42.788 --> 00:23:45.951
I'd love to, but I
already have a date.

00:23:46.091 --> 00:23:47.353
Who with?

00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:48.688
The Captain.

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:50.955
She's invited me
to her quarters for dinner.

00:23:51.096 --> 00:23:52.961
In six years, I have
never been invited

00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:54.963
to the Captain's
quarters for dinner.

00:23:55.033 --> 00:23:56.728
Well, I'll give her
your regards.

00:24:04.543 --> 00:24:06.636
Oh, damn!

00:24:08.213 --> 00:24:09.305
Come in.

00:24:11.883 --> 00:24:13.908
Formal dress
wasn't required, Ensign.

00:24:14.052 --> 00:24:17.544
Well, I just... I figured
dinner with the Captain...

00:24:17.622 --> 00:24:19.089
I'd hardly call this dinner.

00:24:19.157 --> 00:24:21.648
My replicator decided
to liquefy the pot roast.

00:24:21.726 --> 00:24:23.921
It looks fine to me.

00:24:23.995 --> 00:24:25.724
Stop trying
to get on my good side

00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:27.162
and grab a slice of bread.

00:24:27.232 --> 00:24:29.462
Peanut butter
and jelly sandwiches.

00:24:29.534 --> 00:24:30.933
I hope you don't mind.

00:24:31.069 --> 00:24:32.331
Not at all.

00:24:32.404 --> 00:24:34.269
I lived on them at the Academy.

00:24:34.339 --> 00:24:36.933
So, how was your first day
back on the job?

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:38.508
Pretty good, I think.

00:24:38.577 --> 00:24:41.341
Lieutenant Torres called
my work "competent."

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:44.871
Trust me, that's high praise
coming from B'Elanna.

00:24:48.253 --> 00:24:51.381
Commander Tuvok finished
his analysis of your shuttle

00:24:51.456 --> 00:24:53.720
and presented me
with 37 different ways

00:24:53.792 --> 00:24:55.521
of repelling a Kobali attack.

00:24:55.594 --> 00:24:57.824
Did he include your pot roast?

00:24:58.997 --> 00:24:59.964
I'm sorry.

00:25:00.031 --> 00:25:01.623
I didn't mean...

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:04.294
I can't believe
I just said that.

00:25:04.369 --> 00:25:05.631
Why? It was funny.

00:25:05.704 --> 00:25:07.365
We're not on the Bridge,
Lyndsay.

00:25:07.439 --> 00:25:09.304
You have permission
to speak freely.

00:25:09.374 --> 00:25:11.433
Do you really mean that?

00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:14.138
I wouldn't
have said it otherwise.

00:25:14.212 --> 00:25:17.340
Then... there's something
I've wanted to ask you

00:25:17.415 --> 00:25:18.882
for a long time.

00:25:20.519 --> 00:25:22.851
Why me?

00:25:22.921 --> 00:25:24.912
I'm sorry?

00:25:25.023 --> 00:25:27.924
Why did you choose me
for that away mission?

00:25:27.993 --> 00:25:31.656
Well, I suppose I thought you
were best suited for the job.

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:34.358
No, I wasn't.

00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:35.660
Dilithium extraction

00:25:35.734 --> 00:25:38.601
was always Lieutenant Torres'
specialty.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:40.934
And Tuvok had
far more experience

00:25:41.006 --> 00:25:42.701
conducting away missions,

00:25:42.774 --> 00:25:44.708
but you didn't send
either one of them.

00:25:44.776 --> 00:25:47.370
Was it because
they were closer to you?

00:25:49.414 --> 00:25:50.847
You blame me.

00:25:50.916 --> 00:25:53.146
No. No, that's not what I meant.

00:25:53.218 --> 00:25:54.515
- It's okay, Lyndsay.
- No, it's not.

00:25:54.586 --> 00:25:55.848
I'm not offended.

00:25:55.921 --> 00:25:57.821
No, you d...
you don't understand.

00:25:59.524 --> 00:26:03.051
"Never harbor anger toward those
who brought you death,

00:26:03.128 --> 00:26:06.029
for they gave you the chance
to live again."

00:26:06.097 --> 00:26:11.228
In letting me die, Captain,
you gave me life.

00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:16.507
I'm sorry.

00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:17.337
Lyndsay...

00:26:17.409 --> 00:26:18.341
I'm sorry.

00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:19.536
I shouldn't have come.

00:26:31.957 --> 00:26:33.424
You're late.

00:26:33.491 --> 00:26:35.516
We expected you hours ago.

00:26:35.594 --> 00:26:36.526
For what?

00:26:36.595 --> 00:26:37.857
Your farewell party.

00:26:37.929 --> 00:26:39.726
You weren't supposed
to come back.

00:26:39.798 --> 00:26:41.390
You don't belong here anymore.

00:26:41.466 --> 00:26:42.933
Harry, what's going on?

00:26:43.001 --> 00:26:44.935
"Lyndsay Ballard, beloved friend

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:46.867
and crewman"...
does that sound right?

00:26:46.938 --> 00:26:48.235
What?

00:26:48.306 --> 00:26:49.603
For your eulogy...

00:26:49.674 --> 00:26:51.198
does that sound okay?

00:26:51.276 --> 00:26:53.301
Harry, I'm not dead.

00:26:53.378 --> 00:26:56.313
Denial: One of the final stages.

00:26:56.381 --> 00:26:59.145
It was illogical for you
to return.

00:27:00.619 --> 00:27:03.782
Please, I don't want to go.

00:27:03.855 --> 00:27:05.846
I couldn't save
you before, Lyndsay.

00:27:05.924 --> 00:27:08.222
What makes you think
I can save you now?

00:27:11.262 --> 00:27:15.323
Jen'to ka'siote... Jhet'leya.

00:27:23.942 --> 00:27:25.375
Come in.

00:27:31.049 --> 00:27:32.914
What's wrong?

00:27:33.051 --> 00:27:34.916
Bad day, I guess.

00:27:35.053 --> 00:27:37.920
B'Elanna told me
you did great in Engineering.

00:27:38.056 --> 00:27:39.853
I solved a simple problem.

00:27:39.924 --> 00:27:41.915
Didn't sound so simple to me.

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:45.518
Any Kobali can discern
simple wave distortions.

00:27:45.597 --> 00:27:49.931
Even if B'Elanna was impressed,
the others were staring at me.

00:27:50.068 --> 00:27:52.434
I'm sure it was
just your imagination.

00:27:52.504 --> 00:27:54.369
And then, to make
matters worse,

00:27:54.439 --> 00:27:56.930
I started babbling
in front of the Captain.

00:27:57.008 --> 00:27:59.977
Oh. I used to get pretty
nervous around her, too.

00:28:01.379 --> 00:28:02.869
Yeah, don't worry.

00:28:02.981 --> 00:28:05.472
I'm sure she didn't
take it personally.

00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:10.582
Hey...

00:28:12.624 --> 00:28:14.592
I know this isn't easy...

00:28:16.528 --> 00:28:18.655
but I'll help you through this.

00:28:21.866 --> 00:28:25.893
You have always been
far too nice to me.

00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:27.471
Why is that?

00:28:31.376 --> 00:28:34.402
You really don't have
any idea, do you?

00:28:36.214 --> 00:28:38.011
Think about it.

00:28:38.083 --> 00:28:40.916
I rearranged my schedule
at the Academy

00:28:41.019 --> 00:28:43.681
just so we'd be
in the same classes.

00:28:43.755 --> 00:28:48.351
I let you teach me how to skate,
even though I hate the cold.

00:28:50.562 --> 00:28:53.087
I'm crazy about you.

00:28:53.164 --> 00:28:56.190
I have been
since the day we met.

00:28:56.267 --> 00:28:58.895
Why didn't you ever tell me?

00:29:01.506 --> 00:29:04.532
I was never good
at public speaking, remember?

00:29:07.512 --> 00:29:11.471
But I figure how often
do you get a second chance.

00:29:13.017 --> 00:29:17.420
Which is why I'd very much
like to kiss you now.

00:29:22.026 --> 00:29:23.516
"Own the Day."

00:29:48.787 --> 00:29:51.255
Sorry.

00:29:51.322 --> 00:29:53.483
You are creating disorder.

00:29:53.558 --> 00:29:55.253
Seven will be angry.

00:29:55.326 --> 00:29:57.055
I don't care.

00:30:04.569 --> 00:30:05.934
They're cubes.

00:30:06.070 --> 00:30:07.469
I can see that.

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:10.872
Precisely 1/1,000
the size of a Borg vessel.

00:30:10.942 --> 00:30:12.409
Well done.

00:30:14.913 --> 00:30:17.939
A 26-sided polyhedron,
composed of hexagons,

00:30:18.049 --> 00:30:20.711
octagons and squares.

00:30:20.785 --> 00:30:22.753
Impressive.

00:30:28.092 --> 00:30:29.525
What's this?

00:30:29.594 --> 00:30:31.221
Can't you tell?

00:30:33.264 --> 00:30:35.061
It's you.

00:30:35.133 --> 00:30:38.398
I don't see the resemblance.

00:30:38.469 --> 00:30:39.299
Look.

00:30:39.370 --> 00:30:41.133
Here's your ocular implant,

00:30:41.206 --> 00:30:42.468
your nose,

00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:43.871
your mouth...

00:30:43.942 --> 00:30:45.967
You were instructed to create
a geometric shape.

00:30:46.044 --> 00:30:47.306
I reminded her of that.

00:30:47.378 --> 00:30:49.141
She wouldn't comply.

00:30:49.214 --> 00:30:50.841
This was more fun.

00:30:54.252 --> 00:30:55.844
Don't you like it?

00:30:55.920 --> 00:30:58.480
It is crude.

00:31:00.058 --> 00:31:04.518
However, it does demonstrate
ingenuity and individuality.

00:31:04.596 --> 00:31:06.621
She deviated
from your instructions.

00:31:06.698 --> 00:31:10.691
Aren't you going to implement
a punishment protocol?

00:31:12.570 --> 00:31:14.037
No.

00:31:16.708 --> 00:31:18.903
Resume your disorder.

00:31:27.752 --> 00:31:29.219
Lyndsay?

00:31:31.589 --> 00:31:33.557
They're coming.

00:31:39.597 --> 00:31:40.894
Red Alert.

00:31:40.965 --> 00:31:41.897
Raise shields.

00:31:41.966 --> 00:31:44.366
We are being hailed.

00:31:44.435 --> 00:31:45.561
On screen.

00:31:46.838 --> 00:31:48.738
I've come for Jhet'leya.

00:31:48.806 --> 00:31:50.603
If you're referring
to Ensign Ballard,

00:31:50.675 --> 00:31:53.576
she's made it clear that she
doesn't want to go with you.

00:31:53.645 --> 00:31:55.112
She's my daughter.

00:31:56.648 --> 00:32:00.482
Please... I've come a long way.

00:32:00.551 --> 00:32:03.111
I only want to speak with her.

00:32:09.427 --> 00:32:11.088
You don't have
to see him, you know.

00:32:11.162 --> 00:32:12.424
They can't make you.

00:32:12.497 --> 00:32:14.897
I want to, Harry.

00:32:14.966 --> 00:32:17.400
It's time to stop running.

00:32:20.471 --> 00:32:22.439
I appreciate this, Captain.

00:32:22.507 --> 00:32:23.804
I'm willing to oblige

00:32:23.875 --> 00:32:27.106
as long as you understand
that this meeting is over

00:32:27.178 --> 00:32:29.703
as soon as Ensign Ballard
says it is.

00:32:31.249 --> 00:32:33.683
What have they done to you?

00:32:33.751 --> 00:32:35.776
Given me my life back.

00:32:35.853 --> 00:32:38.048
You were so beautiful.

00:32:41.426 --> 00:32:43.451
It's good to see you, Jhet'leya.

00:32:43.528 --> 00:32:45.189
My name is Lyndsay.

00:32:45.263 --> 00:32:48.460
Why did you leave us?

00:32:48.533 --> 00:32:50.933
I wanted to be
with my people again.

00:32:51.002 --> 00:32:51.969
These people?

00:32:52.103 --> 00:32:54.537
The same ones who set you
adrift in space?

00:32:54.605 --> 00:32:58.371
We jettisoned her body
in accordance with our customs.

00:32:58.443 --> 00:32:59.740
You abandoned her.

00:32:59.811 --> 00:33:02.814
You had no right
to tamper with her remains.

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:06.077
We were acting in accordance
with our customs.

00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:07.344
You mutilated her.

00:33:07.418 --> 00:33:08.510
Ensign...

00:33:09.587 --> 00:33:11.145
The reanimation process

00:33:11.222 --> 00:33:14.282
usually results in
extensive memory loss,

00:33:14.359 --> 00:33:17.453
which makes the transition
less painful.

00:33:17.528 --> 00:33:20.326
Unfortunately, some remember

00:33:20.398 --> 00:33:22.696
their former lives
more than others.

00:33:22.767 --> 00:33:24.325
Jhet'leya, for example.

00:33:24.402 --> 00:33:26.597
I told you to call me...

00:33:26.671 --> 00:33:28.036
Lyndsay Ballard.

00:33:28.106 --> 00:33:29.368
She's dead.

00:33:29.440 --> 00:33:33.536
She has been for three years.

00:33:33.611 --> 00:33:36.102
Forgive me for being so blunt,

00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:40.480
but when we found her,
she was a lifeless corpse.

00:33:40.551 --> 00:33:45.215
We salvaged that raw material
to create a new person...

00:33:45.289 --> 00:33:47.621
my daughter... whom I love.

00:33:47.692 --> 00:33:49.421
I'm not your daughter.

00:33:49.494 --> 00:33:52.486
You may have altered
your appearance,

00:33:52.563 --> 00:33:55.464
but do you still think
like these people?

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:59.333
Even now, the first words
that come into your head,

00:33:59.404 --> 00:34:01.872
are they in their language
or mine?

00:34:01.939 --> 00:34:04.840
I realize this place

00:34:04.909 --> 00:34:08.709
is familiar to you,
but it's not where you belong.

00:34:10.415 --> 00:34:12.349
Your sister misses you.

00:34:13.985 --> 00:34:15.009
Tynsia.

00:34:15.086 --> 00:34:19.386
She keeps asking
when you're coming home.

00:34:19.457 --> 00:34:22.119
What should I tell her?

00:34:30.735 --> 00:34:33.568
Tell her that her sister's dead.

00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:40.071
I'll escort you
to the transporter room.

00:34:40.211 --> 00:34:42.338
I won't give her up, Captain.

00:34:42.413 --> 00:34:44.438
She made her wishes clear.

00:34:44.515 --> 00:34:45.880
She's confused.

00:34:45.950 --> 00:34:48.214
Thanks to what you did to her.

00:34:49.754 --> 00:34:51.551
I don't want to fight you.

00:34:51.622 --> 00:34:53.852
Your ship is no match
for Voyager.

00:34:55.726 --> 00:35:00.959
Every life is precious
to my people, Captain.

00:35:01.032 --> 00:35:04.195
I won't be coming back alone.

00:35:16.814 --> 00:35:18.281
Midnight snack?

00:35:22.753 --> 00:35:25.119
Kobali cuisine at its finest.

00:35:27.158 --> 00:35:31.094
So I was giving
some thought to #32...

00:35:31.162 --> 00:35:33.062
"Make Tuvok laugh."

00:35:33.131 --> 00:35:35.759
He has this holo-program,
"The Temple of T'Panit."

00:35:35.833 --> 00:35:37.266
I thought we might tweak it,

00:35:37.335 --> 00:35:40.532
so that instead of Vulcan
prayers, the monks recite

00:35:40.605 --> 00:35:42.402
Ferengi limericks.

00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:46.909
You're not laughing.

00:35:48.513 --> 00:35:50.378
Sorry.

00:35:50.448 --> 00:35:53.076
I can't stop thinking
about Q'ret.

00:35:53.151 --> 00:35:56.245
I can't believe he had the nerve
to call himself your father.

00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:57.651
I'll bet Professor Ballard

00:35:57.722 --> 00:35:59.883
would have had something
to say about that.

00:35:59.957 --> 00:36:02.391
Who?

00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:05.429
Your... dad.

00:36:05.496 --> 00:36:08.192
Doesn't he teach
at some university?

00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:11.495
I don't remember.

00:36:13.838 --> 00:36:16.830
I don't remember
anything about him.

00:36:20.878 --> 00:36:22.743
Let's get down to the holodeck.

00:36:22.813 --> 00:36:25.441
We've got some monks to tweak.

00:36:25.516 --> 00:36:26.778
Sure.

00:36:29.020 --> 00:36:30.419
What's wrong?

00:36:44.769 --> 00:36:47.636
Why did she start to
revert all of a sudden?

00:36:47.705 --> 00:36:49.297
Our old friend, the pathogen.

00:36:49.373 --> 00:36:51.773
It's adapting
to counteract my treatments.

00:36:51.842 --> 00:36:54.504
It's possible she'll suffer
occasional relapses

00:36:54.579 --> 00:36:55.944
for the rest of her life.

00:36:56.047 --> 00:36:57.878
You said you could
maintain my appearance.

00:36:57.949 --> 00:36:59.940
I can, but it looks like
I'll need to increase

00:37:00.017 --> 00:37:01.450
the frequency
of your treatments.

00:37:01.519 --> 00:37:03.419
You'll have to see me
at least twice a day.

00:37:03.487 --> 00:37:07.617
How am I supposed to do my job
if I'm in here all the time?

00:37:07.692 --> 00:37:09.887
How am I supposed
to do anything?

00:37:10.027 --> 00:37:11.051
Please try to underst...

00:37:11.128 --> 00:37:12.595
Stoi'gia!

00:37:12.663 --> 00:37:14.597
Net'staika pen'daeli shevaob!

00:37:17.868 --> 00:37:19.028
I'm sorry.

00:37:37.088 --> 00:37:38.248
Wow.

00:37:40.091 --> 00:37:41.820
This place sure is lived-in.

00:37:41.892 --> 00:37:44.827
If you're here to lecture
me about cleanliness...

00:37:44.895 --> 00:37:49.025
I'm here to ask you
to stop the treatments.

00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:51.898
You know what happens if I do.

00:37:51.969 --> 00:37:53.436
You'll look Kobali again?

00:37:53.504 --> 00:37:54.664
So what?

00:37:56.707 --> 00:37:57.901
I thought you were cute bald.

00:38:00.244 --> 00:38:01.404
I don't care

00:38:01.479 --> 00:38:03.413
if you're human,
Kobali or Bolian.

00:38:03.481 --> 00:38:05.073
I just want you to be happy.

00:38:06.484 --> 00:38:07.781
I wouldn't fit in.

00:38:07.852 --> 00:38:10.446
Are you saying Tuvok
and Neelix don't fit in?

00:38:10.521 --> 00:38:11.647
That's different.

00:38:11.722 --> 00:38:13.713
They got to grow up
in their own cultures.

00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:15.986
They know where they
come from, who they are.

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:17.618
Wherever they come from,

00:38:17.695 --> 00:38:20.789
they're part of this crew now,
just like you.

00:38:20.865 --> 00:38:22.423
Lyndsay was part of this crew.

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:25.333
If I stop the treatments,
I won't be Lyndsay anymore.

00:38:25.403 --> 00:38:27.701
You don't honestly believe that.

00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:34.273
Since the day I got back here,
I haven't felt right.

00:38:34.345 --> 00:38:36.336
First I thought it was Voyager.

00:38:36.414 --> 00:38:38.041
Things had changed so much,

00:38:38.115 --> 00:38:40.675
I thought if I just
gave myself more time

00:38:40.751 --> 00:38:43.345
I'd get used to it.

00:38:43.421 --> 00:38:45.685
But it's me.

00:38:45.756 --> 00:38:48.520
I've changed.

00:38:50.561 --> 00:38:55.157
And the more I try to deny it,
the more I feel like a ghost.

00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:05.372
I'm sorry, Harry...

00:39:05.443 --> 00:39:08.207
but I can't
keep fighting anymore.

00:39:08.279 --> 00:39:10.804
What about us?

00:39:12.516 --> 00:39:17.647
The girl you were in love with
died three years ago.

00:39:26.797 --> 00:39:29.322
Shields down to 48 percent.

00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:31.061
Target the lead ship's
weapons array.

00:39:31.135 --> 00:39:35.003
Life support's failing
on Decks 6 through 10.

00:39:35.072 --> 00:39:37.199
Reroute power to compensate.

00:39:37.274 --> 00:39:39.071
Shields at 20 percent.

00:39:39.143 --> 00:39:40.906
Hail them.
Tell them you'll surrender me.

00:39:41.011 --> 00:39:43.172
Don't listen to her, Captain.

00:39:43.247 --> 00:39:44.714
I appreciate the gesture,
Lyndsay,

00:39:44.782 --> 00:39:46.010
but I'm not giving you up.

00:39:46.083 --> 00:39:47.914
It's not a gesture.
I want to go.

00:39:48.052 --> 00:39:49.417
I don't belong here.

00:39:49.487 --> 00:39:50.749
She's not well.

00:39:50.821 --> 00:39:52.049
She doesn't know
what she's saying.

00:39:52.123 --> 00:39:55.058
I know exactly what I'm saying.

00:39:55.126 --> 00:39:56.218
Shields at 13 percent.

00:39:56.293 --> 00:39:58.090
I'm detecting power

00:39:58.162 --> 00:40:00.221
fluctuations
in the lead vessel's warp drive.

00:40:00.297 --> 00:40:02.595
A polaron burst
could overload the core.

00:40:02.666 --> 00:40:04.258
That would destroy the ship.

00:40:04.335 --> 00:40:06.269
They're not leaving
us much choice.

00:40:06.337 --> 00:40:09.329
Whatever we do,
we have to do it fast.

00:40:10.441 --> 00:40:12.409
You're sure
this is what you want.

00:40:12.476 --> 00:40:16.537
Captain, I can fire
that polaron burst myself.

00:40:16.614 --> 00:40:17.740
Stand down, Ensign.

00:40:17.815 --> 00:40:19.680
We can't just let them take her!

00:40:21.585 --> 00:40:24.679
Even if you stop them,
I can't stay on Voyager.

00:40:24.755 --> 00:40:27.121
I don't want to lose you.

00:40:27.191 --> 00:40:29.659
You already did,
but at least this time,

00:40:29.727 --> 00:40:32.457
we've been given the chance
to say good-bye.

00:40:36.667 --> 00:40:40.967
Captain's Log, Stardate 53679.4.

00:40:41.105 --> 00:40:43.733
The Doctor has stopped
Ensign Ballard's treatments,

00:40:43.808 --> 00:40:45.105
and her Kobali physiology

00:40:45.176 --> 00:40:47.303
is already beginning
to reassert itself.

00:40:47.378 --> 00:40:49.869
All but one of us
have said our good-byes.

00:41:02.660 --> 00:41:05.128
Vien'ke debala, Jhet'leya.

00:41:06.197 --> 00:41:09.189
I taught myself
to say a few words in Kobali.

00:41:09.266 --> 00:41:11.200
That's very sweet of you,

00:41:11.268 --> 00:41:15.068
but you just told me
the comets are tiresome.

00:41:17.074 --> 00:41:19.941
Guess I better work
on my pronunciation.

00:41:20.077 --> 00:41:21.908
I'm sorry
you didn't get to finish

00:41:21.979 --> 00:41:23.276
everything on your list.

00:41:30.421 --> 00:41:33.049
I think I took care of
what really mattered.

00:42:15.065 --> 00:42:16.362
That's pretty.

00:42:19.069 --> 00:42:21.037
It belonged to a friend of mine.

00:42:27.077 --> 00:42:28.544
Would you like it?

00:42:28.612 --> 00:42:31.410
Your friend wouldn't mind?

00:42:31.482 --> 00:42:32.949
I think she'd be happy

00:42:33.050 --> 00:42:36.577
knowing I gave it to someone
with such pretty hair.

00:42:38.756 --> 00:42:42.624
Seven's letting us go
to the holodeck by ourselves.

00:42:42.693 --> 00:42:45.685
She says we can run
any program we want.

00:42:45.763 --> 00:42:47.526
Do you want to come?

00:42:47.598 --> 00:42:51.034
Have you ever heard
of "The Temple of T'Panit"?

00:42:52.670 --> 00:42:54.137
It's a Vulcan program.

00:42:54.204 --> 00:42:56.365
Sounds boring.

00:42:56.440 --> 00:42:57.634
Don't worry.

00:42:57.708 --> 00:42:59.335
We'll make a few tweaks.
